cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite the released software version."
type: software
title: "Nonlinear Diffusion Interactive Model / Learning App"
version: "2.3"
date-released: 2026-10-01
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Kang
    given-names: Wook
abstract: >-
  A Jupyter-based research software prototype for forward and inverse nonlinear
  diffusion modeling in 1D, 2D, and 3D. It includes isotropic FDM/FVM/FEM
  backends, an axis-aligned diagonal-anisotropic FVM backend, configurable
  initial and boundary conditions, parameter estimation, local sensitivity and
  practical-identifiability diagnostics, and reproducibility-oriented run
  save/load records.
keywords:
  - nonlinear diffusion
  - finite difference method
  - finite volume method
  - finite element method
  - inverse modeling
  - parameter estimation
  - anisotropic diffusion
  - Jupyter
  - reproducible research
